  "live_records": {
    "q-41414": {
      "dom_id": "step-q41414",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/b08b9f51e04c33c56026abe338c9e1353ddff93d502596241b31e994d66a994c.png)\n\nThe graph of a periodic function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. What is the period of this function?",
      "worked_solution": "Note that if we shift the graph $8$ units left or right, the graph remains unchanged.\n\nOn the other hand, if we shift the graph horizontally by any distance other than $8$ (or a multiple of $8$), we get a different graph.\n\nTherefore, the period of the function is $8.$",
